    <summary>Convert PDF to JPG on Windows: this pdf to jpg converter turns each page of one or many files into a separate image at the resolution you choose, rendered offline by a built-in PDF engine.</summary>
    <description>PDF to JPG Converter Software lets an office convert pdf to jpg on its own Windows workstations, page by page, instead of sending invoices and contracts through a website. For admins deploying it with Chocolatey, the useful detail is that the package carries its own PDF rendering engine, so the PCs need no other PDF software and documents stay on the machine.

![PDF to JPG Converter screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/p2j/p2j-v1-main.png)

## How to use the pdf to jpg converter

1. Install the package and open the program from the Start menu. No separate PDF reader or codec is required on the workstation.
2. Select PDF documents with Add Files or Add Folder, or drag them into the list.
3. Pick JPG, PNG, BMP, TIFF or WEBP as the photo format; JPG is preselected.
4. Optionally pick a DPI preset (72, 150, 300 or 600) or a custom value between 60 and 900, and a page range.
5. Select the destination, or save images next to the original PDF, and click Start.

Trial note: the demo version converts within a daily limit and shows a reminder screen until it is registered. A license removes that limit.

![PDF to JPG Converter screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/p2j/p2j-v1-folder.png)

## What a pdf to image converter writes to disk

- A separate picture for every page, so a 30-page PDF converts into 30 images.
- File names built from the PDF name and the page number, such as contract_page_002.jpg, which keeps large jobs in order.
- Adjustable JPEG quality and compression, with a black and white option, so a page with a high-quality photo can stay sharp or a text page can stay small.
- Convert PDF to PNG instead of JPEG when a page has fine lines or text that should not blur.
- A recreated folder structure when you process a tree of subfolders.
- Multipage TIFF output for archives that prefer one file per document.

In batch jobs the pdf to image converter uses every CPU core, which matters when a scanner folder holds hundreds of documents. Explorer integration and a command line are included as well. The program does not perform OCR, create PDFs from images or edit documents, so a separate tool is needed for those tasks.

## Who needs to convert PDF to JPG

- Accounting teams that forward a single invoice page.
- Marketing staff who publish catalog and brochure pages as JPG photos on a website.
- Support desks that attach a page as an image to a ticket.
- Admins who want an offline PDF to JPG tool on shared PCs, tested on Windows 10 and Windows 11.

![PDF to JPG Converter screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/p2j/p2j-v1-done.png)

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of PDF to JPG Converter Software, a commercial program from SoftOrbits. Full use without the daily conversion limit requires a license. Lifetime, 1-year and business plans are available at [PDF to JPG Converter](https://www.softorbits.net/pdf-to-jpg-converter/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package).

## FAQ

### How do I change a multi-page PDF into separate JPG files?

Add it to the list and press Start. Every page becomes its own JPG, numbered in page order.

### Do PCs need Acrobat installed to turn a PDF into JPG?

No. This pdf to image converter renders pages with the engine bundled in the package, so Acrobat is not needed on any machine.

### Can I convert PDF to JPG from a phone?

No, the program runs on Windows 10 and Windows 11 PCs. Move the file to a computer first and run a batch pdf to jpg job there.
